{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Turn and journey for yourselves.</b> This is the way of Arad and Hormah." "<b>And come to the hill-country of the Amorite.</b> As it sounds." "<b>And all its neighbors.</b> Ammon and Moab and Mount Seir." "<b>In the Arabah.</b> This is the plain of the forest." "<b>In the mountain.</b> This is the King's Mountain." "<b>And in the lowland.</b> This is the lowland of the south." "<b>And in the Negev and on the coast.</b> Ashkelon and Gaza and Caesarea and so on, as is found in the Sifrei." "<b>As far as the great river.</b> Because it is mentioned together with the Land of Israel, it calls it 'great' — like the common saying: 'slave of a king, [a] king.' 'Cling to the black [garment] and they will bow to you,' 'draw near to this one and he will give [you] a dinar.' (Shevuot 47)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {7 "The Aramaic popular sayings are rendered literally; their force is that proximity to an esteemed person or thing lends prestige."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:45:24.295991068Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}